.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt SYSCONF-POUDRIERE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm "sysconf poudriere"
.Nd configure poudriere.conf and poudriere.d overlay files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm sysconf
.Cm poudriere
.Op Fl Fl jail Ar name
.Op Fl Fl ports Ar name
.Op Fl Fl tree Ar name
.Op Fl Fl set Ar name
.Op Ar sysrc_argument ...
.Nm sysconf
.Cm poudriere
.Bro Cm make Ns | Ns Cm src Ns | Ns Cm src-env Brc
.Op Fl ceFinNqsvVx
.Op Fl Fl jail Ar name
.Op Fl Fl ports Ar name
.Op Fl Fl tree Ar name
.Op Fl Fl set Ar name
.Op Fl j Ar jail | Fl R Ar dir
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Ar name Ns Op Ns Oo +|- Oc Ns = Ns Ar value
.Ar ...
.Nm sysconf
.Cm poudriere
.Bro Cm make Ns | Ns Cm src Ns | Ns Cm src-env Brc
.Op Fl eFnNqvV
.Op Fl Fl jail Ar name
.Op Fl Fl ports Ar name
.Op Fl Fl tree Ar name
.Op Fl Fl set Ar name
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Fl a
.Nm sysconf
.Cm poudriere
.Bro Cm make Ns | Ns Cm src Ns | Ns Cm src-env Brc
.Op Fl E
.Op Fl Fl jail Ar name
.Op Fl Fl ports Ar name
.Op Fl Fl tree Ar name
.Op Fl Fl set Ar name
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Fl l | L
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Cm poudriere
target of
.Xr sysconf 8
reaches the same files
.Xr poudriere 8
sources.
With no sub-target, it is the
.Pa poudriere.conf
collection, handed to
.Xr sysrc 8
as
.Fl f
files.
The sub-targets are
.Cm make ,
.Cm src ,
and
.Cm src-env .
Each is the matching
.Xr make 1
collection under
.Pa poudriere.d ,
handled by the same engine as
.Xr sysconf-make 8 .
.Pp
A unique prefix of the
.Cm poudriere
keyword is accepted
.Pq Ql p .
A unique prefix of a sub-target is accepted the same way
.Po
.Ql m
selects
.Cm make ;
.Ql s
and
.Ql sr
are ambiguous between
.Cm src
and
.Cm src-env
.Pc .
.Ss poudriere.conf
.Pa poudriere.conf
is
.Xr rc.conf 5 Ns -style
shell written by the administrator;
poudriere never writes it.
The default collection, sourced by every poudriere command, is in order:
.Pa POUDRIERE_ETC/poudriere.conf
if readable
.Pq default Pa /usr/local/etc/poudriere.conf ,
then
.Pa POUDRIERED/poudriere.conf
if readable and not the same file as the first
.Pq default Pa POUDRIERE_ETC/poudriere.d/poudriere.conf .
At least one of those two files must exist.
Honor
.Ev POUDRIERE_ETC
and
.Ev POUDRIERED
when set.
.Pp
When a jail, ports tree, or set is given, the matching files are
appended, in the order
.Xr poudriere 8
uses:
.Bd -unfilled -offset indent
.Pa POUDRIERED/<setname>-poudriere.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<tree>-poudriere.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-poudriere.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<tree>-<setname>-poudriere.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-<tree>-poudriere.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-<setname>-poudriere.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-<tree>-<setname>-poudriere.conf
.Ed
.Pp
An explicit
.Xr sysrc 8
.Fl f
replaces discovery.
.Fl l
and
.Fl L
are handled here and printed one path per line.
For this
.Pa poudriere.conf
collection,
.Fl l
lists each readable file.
.Fl L
lists every location the given jail, tree, and set would consult,
including overlays that do not exist yet.
If no jail, tree, or set is given, the list is the two global
.Pa poudriere.conf
paths.
.Fl E
limits either list to files that exist.
.Fl l
and
.Fl L
take no variable names.
Other arguments except the
.Cm poudriere
keyword itself are handed to
.Xr sysrc 8
verbatim.
A bare
.Ql --
means the next word is a variable in this collection, even when that
word is
.Cm make ,
.Cm src ,
.Cm src-env ,
or a unique prefix of one of those sub-targets.
.Ss make.conf, src.conf, and src-env.conf
These live only under
.Pa POUDRIERED
and use
.Xr make 1
syntax, so they are not mixed into the
.Pa poudriere.conf
sysrc collection.
.Pp
.Cm poudriere make
consults, in the order shown by
.Xr poudriere 8 :
.Bd -unfilled -offset indent
.Pa POUDRIERED/make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<setname>-make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<tree>-make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<tree>-<setname>-make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-<tree>-make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-<setname>-make.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-<tree>-<setname>-make.conf
.Ed
.Pp
.Fl l
always prints the global path, even when that file does not exist:
.Pa POUDRIERED/make.conf
for
.Cm make ,
.Pa POUDRIERED/src.conf
for
.Cm src ,
and
.Pa POUDRIERED/src-env.conf
for
.Cm src-env .
An overlay is printed only when the file exists.
.Fl L
lists every location the given jail, tree, and set would consult,
including files that do not exist yet.
.Cm src
and
.Cm src-env
have no per-tree file, so
.Fl Fl tree
does not add a path to those lists.
.Fl E
limits either list to files that exist, so a missing global is omitted.
On a read, a missing global is skipped and an
overlay is consulted only when the file exists.
Hook-plugin
.Pa make.conf
files are not collected.
.Pp
.Cm poudriere src
follows the shorter list
.Xr poudriere 8
uses when building jails
.Pq global, then set, then jail; no tree :
.Bd -unfilled -offset indent
.Pa POUDRIERED/src.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<setname>-src.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-src.conf
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm poudriere src-env
uses that same order, with
.Pa src-env.conf
in place of
.Pa src.conf :
.Bd -unfilled -offset indent
.Pa POUDRIERED/src-env.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<setname>-src-env.conf
.Pa POUDRIERED/<jailname>-src-env.conf
.Ed
.Pp
An explicit
.Fl f
replaces discovery, as on other
.Nm sysconf
targets.
A name already defined is rewritten in the last file in the
collection that defines it, so the change is not placed where a later
overlay would mask it.
A name defined nowhere is appended to the global file, and that write
creates the global file when it is missing.
A bare
.Ar name
reads, and
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
writes, including
.Ql +=
and
.Ql -= .
Those rules are the
.Dq Assignment syntax
section of
.Xr sysconf 8 .
.Ss Context long options
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl jail Ar name
Poudriere jail name, as in
.Pa <jailname>-make.conf
and the other jail files.
.It Fl Fl ports Ar name , Fl Fl tree Ar name
Poudriere ports tree.
.Fl Fl tree
is an alias of
.Fl Fl ports ;
when both are given, the last wins.
A tree applies to
.Pa poudriere.conf
and the
.Cm make
sub-target.
.Cm src
and
.Cm src-env
ignore it; poudriere does not read a per-tree src file.
.It Fl Fl set Ar name
Poudriere set name.
.El
.Pp
.Fl Fl jail Ns = Ns Ar name
(and the same attached form for the others) is accepted.
These long options are consumed here and never passed to
.Xr sysrc 8
or mistaken for
.Nm sysconf
operands.
They are distinct from
.Fl j
on
.Xr sysconf 8
and
.Xr sysrc 8 ,
which name a running jail.
.Ss Out of scope
Poudriere maintains the following itself, or they are a different format:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa poudriere.d/jails/ , poudriere.d/ports/
One file per property; the whole file is the value.
.It Pa poudriere.d/*-options/
A
.Ev PORT_DBDIR
tree of per-port
.Ql OPTIONS
files, written by
.Ql poudriere options
.Pq Ql make config .
.It Pa poudriere.d/*-blacklist
Port origins, one per line
.Pq with optional Ql @flavor ;
.Ql #
comments.
Not
.Ql name=value .
.It Pa poudriere.d/hooks/
Shell scripts, including plugin
.Pa make.conf
files under
.Pa hooks/plugins/ .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width POUDRIERE_ETC
.It Ev POUDRIERE_ETC
Directory containing
.Pa poudriere.conf
.Pq default Pa /usr/local/etc .
.It Ev POUDRIERED
Overlay directory
.Pq default Pa POUDRIERE_ETC/poudriere.d .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl sysconf poudriere ZPOOL=zroot
.Dl sysconf poudriere --jail 131amd64 PARALLEL_JOBS=8
.Dl sysconf p ZPOOL
.Dl sysconf p -- src
.Dl sysconf poudriere make --jail 131amd64 CFLAGS
.Dl sysconf p m --jail 131amd64 CFLAGS+=-O2
.Dl sysconf poudriere src --set dev WITHOUT_LLVM_BINUTILS=
.Dl sysconf p src-env --jail 131amd64 SRC_ENV_VAR
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr poudriere 8 ,
.Xr sysconf 8 ,
.Xr sysconf-make 8 ,
.Xr sysconf-rc 8 ,
.Xr sysrc 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm sysconf
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
